  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Stakeholders to Respond to Challenges Related to Unmanaged Internal Migration in Madagascar through a Human Security Approach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall purpose of this programme is to extend awareness and usage of the human security approach in response to human insecurities that arise from unmanaged internal migration trends as they interact with and reinforce environmental, governance, and health-related issues in Madagascar.  The programme will do so by 1) enhancing the capacity of targeted entities and stakeholders to formulate and implement human security policies and action-oriented initiatives that address the identified insecurities; and 2) building and promoting partnerships with a broad range of local, national, and international stakeholders for greater support and replication of the human security approach beyond the current programme. By the end of the programme period, stakeholders will be empowered to implement responses to the identified insecurities in a holistic and integrated way.</narrative>
  </description>
